{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil","id":830051,"title":"Not Inherently Evil??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-14T22:52:04-08:00","id":830051,"title":"Not Inherently Evil??","content":"Ok, at the behest of some people's comments in another thread I tracked down the Preview PDF that is available to the public to read the Heroes information. I figured I would read the whole thing just to get a feel for how it works an- HOLY CRAP WHAT THE F*CK IS WRONG WITH YOU PEOPLE?!?!<br /> <br /> As a survivor of mental and emotional abuse from a predator pretending to be a loving family member, what I read horrified me to my core. It seems that, if I was reading it right, Beasts *must* inflict some kind of pain on their neighbors to feed their &quot;special souls&quot;. In essence Beasts are abusers but they seem to justify it by targeting people who 'deserve' it. Oh, god, that is not going to sound familiar to abuse survivors AT ALL.<br /> <br /> Now, I have been playing RPG's since the early-80's. Odds are if a game has come out in the last 30-years or so I've played it. I've played lot of Horror RPG's of various types, I've even played some of the oWoD Black Dog label games and worse. But this game practically requires the players to learn how to and play out doing deep psychological damage and long term mental scarring as part of the basic game mechanic.<br /> <br /> I understand that the authors/moderators (at least the two I have interacted with so far) have a rather non &quot;black and white&quot; sense of morality, but a game where you are tormenting people with your fantastical dragon soul and if people object to it then they are evil bigots who don't understand you seems to be beyond &quot;playing a monster&quot; and possibly reaching &quot;Inherently Evil&quot;. This certainly seems to be beyond where the other &quot;monster&quot; game lines go to. When vampires skew evil, for example, they typically see themselves as apex predators; <i>detached</i> predators. If you look at the Invictus or the Sanctum they have opinions about human masses and not individual people. We still can acknowledge that as an evil perspective but it's sensible. I think it's the fact that Beasts tend to judge their prey on a very personal, often petty scale that would make even a vampire raise an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> As TVTropes puts it, &quot;Beasts <i>cannot</i> avoid their need to feed. Even the weakest of Beasts, those who cling most strongly to their human origins, have a choice: either deliberately find someone and scare them, as appropriate for their Hunger, once per week, or else cause nightmares in random people, which will potentially create some loony who will happily maim, kill and burn innocent bystanders to find and kill them. The &quot;best&quot; Beasts are those who accept their Hunger and find a way to sate it that minimizes the harm they cause, as several sample characters mentioned in the corebook show.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now you can try to justify the seeding of fear and apprehension as a good thing - giving people something to overcome and better themselves, etc - but THAT IS LITERALLY THEY TYPE OF THING THAT REAL-LIFE ABUSERS SAY TO JUSTIFY THEIR ATROCITIES. Even the powers, with names like &quot;Everyone Hates You,&quot; &quot;You Deserve This,&quot; and &quot;Everything You Do is Worthless&quot; read like the a laundry-list of psychosis-causing phraseology. The players know from the very beginning that they are truly evil creatures intended to cause horror, regardless of how they try to justify it or minimize their harm. Heroes, for all their fanaticism and flaws, are trying to stop a self-admitted monster from spreading nightmares across... well.. everywhere but somehow Beasts have the moral high ground?<br /> <br /> At least one poster in the other threat suggested that Beasts, while monsters, could be heroes. Having now read the book I literally do not see how that is possible. I may be missing something but this might as well have been called Sadist: the Abuser instead. Now, I will admit that, given my background, I am not exactly coming to this game with no baggage. SO...<br /> <br /> Explain to me how sounds like a fun experience which will totally not bring the wrong kind of attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":11143,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","user":"Feonorx","date":". 02-15-2016, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T23:51:21-08:00","id":830067,"title":"","content":"Do you actually want someone to try to justify a heroic Beast? Because based on your post, it sounds to me like you have your mind pretty firmly made up against the possibility of such a thing. <br /> <br /> Assuming you actually are open to the possibility of a heroic Beast character, I submit the following:<br /> Ugallu Predator. His Hunger is the actual predation sort of predator. Not a social predator, but a literal predator. He feels an instinctive urge to hunt and chase. He doesn't want to hurt anyone, so he keeps his Satiety low and goes on hunting trips when necessary, keeping himself fed by killing a deer or a rabbit or a duck or something. He probably uses the meat to feed his body's more ordinary form of hunger. His hunger thus sated, he goes about his life. ... which, since he's supposed to be a hero, probably involves taking care of orphans or making sure his neighborhood is safe from Unfriendly Neighborhood Vampires or something.<br /> <br /> I suppose you could also do something with a Predator who works with a Hunter cell and literally feeds by helping them to hunt down hostile supernatural threats that are preying on innocent people. Slashers, zombies, angry ghosts, the occasional vampire or werewolf, that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T00:32:03-08:00","id":830075,"title":"","content":"You're pretty clearly looking at the preview draft, which lacks some of the revisions that adjusted things \u2014 Heroes are no longer created by Beasts, for instance \u2014 but for brevity's sake (and in the interest of not losing too much sleep on the night before an early shift) I'm going to just quote the Themes section of the backer copy of the full book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No Neat Little Boxes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are not \u201cgood guys.\u201d They terrify people in order to feed their Horrors. Although their culture teaches that they do so in order to impart important lessons, their peculiar form of pedagogy is entirely optional. A Beast is capable of being a force for wisdom, even for \u201cgood\u201d in the World of Darkness, but doing so is entirely up to the Beast. <b>Likewise, a Beast primary enemy, the Hero, believes that killing the Beast is the right, objectively moral thing to do. The Beast disagrees. <u>Neither of them is necessarily wrong</u></b>.<br /> <br /> A kind of dichotomy \u2014 the Beast and the Human \u2014 is an integral part of Beast. That isn\u2019t to suggest any kind of reconciliation; a Beast can never be fully human. Perhaps, though, Humanity is just one more type of monster; the fact that <u>any</u> human can become a Beast is an important part of that. That applies to many of the other types of supernatural being (anyone can theoretically become a vampire, mage, changeling, or Sin-Eater, too, since those conditions are all foisted upon people from the outside), but for a Beast, the potential to become the monster is right there, in the deepest, darkest part of humanity\u2019s nightmares, locked into their very genetic code. <b>The characters in Beast are not the most evil parts of humanity. They\u2019re the <u>scariest</u> parts of humanity, because they are the stuff of nightmares.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>You Don't Choose Your Family</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monsters don\u2019t choose to be monsters, <u>but</u>, looking at Greek myths, one often finds an element of fatalism or determinism. Medusa and her sisters are sometimes listed as children of Echidna, but there are also legends that Athena cursed Medusa for sleeping with Poseidon. <b>That notion that monsters are responsible for their own nature plays into the rather childish, but pervasive, notion that everyone and everything faces the same choices. On a sociopolitical level, we see it when people blame the poor for being poor, as though it was a choice (and a moral failing). In Beast, Heroes see the Begotten as irredeemable because of what they are \u2014 but the Beasts cannot be otherwise. </b>Even Beasts that \u201cchoose\u201d to be Beasts because another of their kind offered the Devouring aren\u2019t really making a choice; they know what they are. The Devouring just confirms it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>To Thine Own Self Be True</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are primal, elemental, and ultimately simple, right? The Horror is, at least. An individual Beast might have a job, friends, family, lovers, children, and all the while they are also a powerful and hungry being from the nightmares of early humanity. They cannot ignore the Horror, or it runs wild through local dreams and attracts the notice of heroes. They cannot ignore the human part of their lives, or they slowly lose touch with the world and become cruel and savage. <b>Beasts have to be true to themselves, but being true to themselves doesn\u2019t excuse them from the consequences.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T00:59:14-08:00","id":830084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830067#post830067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you actually want someone to try to justify a heroic Beast? Because based on your post, it sounds to me like you have your mind pretty firmly made up against the possibility of such a thing..</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually would like somebody to justify psychological damage as a game mechanic, more than a heroic Beast. <br /> <br /> I want somebody to explain how it would be a &quot;fun&quot; game to break even an NPC down physically, emotionally and/or psychologically in the manner described in the book. For example, from the book: &quot;Darius took his name and his hunting style from a werewolf he met once. He chases down his prey and breaks a bone \u2014 arm, leg, neck, doesn\u2019t matter, as long as he can hear the crack. He inflicts pain and fear in his prey and leaves behind a crippled, terrified person\u2026or sometimes just a corpse, depending on how loudly his Soul howls.&quot; Even the Slashers game didn't go this far. So tell me how playing this sadistic torture is a &quot;fun roleplaying experience&quot; and not &quot;Inherently Evil&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for your example, I not sure that what you describe would work per the rules, as he is not Satiating on people. Further, if that counts as heroism, I'm not sure we are working off the same definitions. Perhaps if he used his instinctive urge to hunt and chase on Vampires, evil cultists, or what-have-you then maybe... but would he be generating sufficient terror to fill the Hunger? Not sure it would work...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T01:04:21-08:00","id":830086,"title":"","content":"I've had beasts in my game that didn't hurt or abuse anyone, and I've still only seen the preview version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So tell me how playing this sadistic torture is a &quot;fun roleplaying experience&quot; and not &quot;Inherently Evil&quot;. </div> </div> </div>1. You don't have to be sadistic.<br /> 2. You don't have to torture anyone. You can do something as simple as intimidating a guy who was acting disrespectful to a waitress, or as a politician you decommission a building that people loved, or just having some supernatural friends.<br /> 3. One of the points is to figureout ways to feed your hunger without committing horrible acts. You can maintain your morality, but it will make your horror ravenous. Which will also increase some of your powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-15-2016, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T01:22:07-08:00","id":830089,"title":"","content":"As an aside, I remember when the game came out and a lot of people took it as a metaphor for sexuality. Now it's getting compared to abuse dynamics. Both are interesting angles.<br /> <br /> I think OP's not too far off the mark - I mean, yes, horrors NEED to be fed, and fear is their bread and butter. But there are a couple of nuances which I think are important:<br /> - Abusers use made up excuses. A Beat's one is real. This does not make the consequences less disgusting - but the Beast HAS to feed.<br /> - Feeding on the same victim again and again is discouraged. I think there is a difference between long term abuse and a once off burst of fear inflicted on (in all likelihood) a stranger.<br /> - Beasts have absolutely no requirement to like who they are or what they do. Indeed, two of the inheritances are what I see as escape routes, killing off the human bit to make the horror either a purely spiritual nightmare, or an actual monster.<br /> - 'Heroes' are 'wrong', in that their desire to kill beasts is lead by a form of megalomania. But regular people just defending themselves - nothing wrong there, or right either.<br /> - There - are - worst things than Beasts out there, which are worse the hard lessons they teach. Being frightened off by a horror once might be worth it if it prevents one from becoming addicted to being fed on by a vampire, or torn to pieces by a werewolf on her territory. The World of Darkness is a generally shitty place for mortals - so while Beasts certainly aren't good news, they're not necessarily the worst option.<br /> - The whole &quot;lesson teaching&quot; aspect, as presented in the final PDF, is a way for Beast to make the most out of a bad situation. It clearly states the Horror doesn't care about the lesson - but Beasts themselves try to make themselves into something at least marginally better.<br /> - The nightmares' horrible names are just that - they're terrifying because they're relevant psychological fear. But by definition they're inflicted through supernatural means, and temporary.<br /> <br /> To conclude, here are a couple of feeding examples from my campaign which, while not necessarily heroic, are at least different from abuse in my mind:<br /> - Threatening a tyrannical manager with a lawsuit, to stop her from tormenting an employee (Power)<br /> - Creating a victim free incident at an oil drill, to have it shut down and protect the local eco-system (Ruin)<br /> - Buying a coin from a salesman who didn't realize its true value (Hoard)<br /> - Hunting down a werewolf hunter who was about to shoot a pack and their immediate family/friends (Predator)<br /> - Punishing a ghoul who was trying to sneak on the brood's home base to murder them (Punishment)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T01:25:51-08:00","id":830091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830075#post830075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're pretty clearly looking at the preview draft, which lacks some of the revisions that adjusted things \u2014 Heroes are no longer created by Beasts, for instance \u2014 but for brevity's sake (and in the interest of not losing too much sleep on the night before an early shift) I'm going to just quote the Themes section of the backer copy of the full book:</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very glad to hear it. I can understand how things change going from draft to published. I'll give it the benefit of the doubt until the finished work comes out. <br /> <br /> I understand I am not coming into this fairly, given my personal history. But seeing some of the things in the Preview edition - the descriptions, the self-serving justifications - made it hard to finish reading it. let alone evaluate the crunchy bits. I know AnimeArt (if I recall his forum name correctly) is all about the CroD being about monsters... but I believe there are some things that are too monstrous to play out in a game. Hopefully the final version pulls back from this line a bit. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T01:26:43-08:00","id":830092,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> : funny, the waitress thing happened in the very first scene of my campaign.<br /> <br /> Also, if you want a popular example of a heroic beast... there's Batman. The man uses fear as his weapon, to discourage crime. It's his tool, and he probably gets off on it way more than he should - but at the end of the day, if it keeps criminals from doing worse things, it can be counted as a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T01:39:17-08:00","id":830098,"title":"","content":"I thnk you make some very good points, and the feeding examples are quite interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830089#post830089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Feeding on the same victim again and again is discouraged. I think there is a difference between long term abuse and a once off burst of fear inflicted on (in all likelihood) a stranger.<br /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite sure I agree, but I can see where you are coming from in regards to the game.<br /> <br /> Speaking of sexual - it is a strange comparison, but I sometimes feel that the gaming community would benefit from the 3 cardinal rules of the BDSM community: Safe, Sane and Consensual. While you can't exactly have a consensual &quot;monster feeding&quot; situation, you can present it in a safe, sane way, if that makes sense... <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T02:11:35-08:00","id":830105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Feonorx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830091#post830091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm very glad to hear it. I can understand how things change going from draft to published. I'll give it the benefit of the doubt until the finished work comes out.<br /> <br /> I understand I am not coming into this fairly, given my personal history. But seeing some of the things in the Preview edition - the descriptions, the self-serving justifications - made it hard to finish reading it. let alone evaluate the crunchy bits. I know AnimeArt (if I recall his forum name correctly) is all about the CroD being about monsters... but I believe there are some things that are too monstrous to play out in a game. Hopefully the final version pulls back from this line a bit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Im a survivor of teenage sexual abuse myself from a &quot;friend and mentor&quot; , and I dont have a problem with Beast. They try to teach the world teaching wisdom such as &quot;Over coming hardship&quot; or &quot;This too shall pass&quot; ... in a mostly vampire game im running on rpol , the sole beast player is now teaching the world a lesson &quot;Try robbing people, and you'll die under mysterious circumstances&quot; most beasts take this responsiblety seriously and will hunt down themselves someone who takes their mayhem too far.<br /> <br /> am backer of the kickstarter so allready have the PDF, its compelling, though yes I can see how it could be read unfortunately...<br /> <br /> as for how to justify a Heroic beast? Simple<br /> <br /> &quot;You go around targetting Scammers&quot;<br /> <br /> (suggested this to a ST he suggested a Hero from the nigerian royal family as an antaganist... would that be symnetrical? or silly, the REAL nigerian royal family why would they care. came up with the idea after having to reformate my hard drive after being mentally retarded enough to give some jokers access to it because they claimed to work for microsoft.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 02-15-2016, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:19:42-08:00","id":830122,"title":"","content":"Nope, not doing this again, not if you start with that tone and accusations. I hated it in the Kickstarter, I hated it every single time it happened again and I hate it now. I understand emotional baggage and all but that's just counterproductive.<br /> <br /> Bullet points:<br /> <br /> - You're not forced to enjoy the effect you have on people, and never were<br /> - The thing about &quot;I do this to people but it's ok because I say they deserved it?&quot;. It's a possible rationale but it's not the ultimate excuse, nor the only one, nor an absolute that's objectively valid and again, it NEVER was<br /> - The Horror is a monster, the Beast does not have to<br /> - The fact that a Beast has to do unpleasant thing to survive does not mean that those things have no consequences nor that Beasts are excusable<br /> - The types of action you need to feed are not only variables of torture, psychological or not. There's plenty of ways, not to mention the fact that you can tag along supernaturals that do their thing and feed by merely being there.<br /> - Tv Tropes, as much as it can be useful, is made by all sorts of people with no limitations and it's not the final judge nor impartially correct by default on anything.<br /> - The revised book offers indeed a more positive role for Beasts in the world if they choose to take it and deals with many of the most problematic points (or at least those who were dangerously open to negative, and I guess legitimate, interpretations)<br /> - The point, <b>and I mean the main source of drama of the whole game</b>, is to find a balance with your horrifying needs and your own morale. It can be difficult, it can be easy, but it's that.<br /> <br /> The Beasts I've enjoyed more making are those who try to do good no matter what their monstrous nature demands. And the fact is, they're not oddities: they're the actual norm. Merging with a Horror does not make your morality disappear. Beasts are people, with alle the negatives and positives meanings of the term, and that means they can as bad or as good as you want them.<br /> <br /> The people who love this game are not assholes, nor sociopaths nor abuse justifiers. And every single time we have to justify ourselves in front of someone who comes around and begins by making a certain type of assumption seasoned with a variable amount of bile, I cannot help but to think that they've read the book (yes, even the preview, which <b>I completely agree</b> had to be revised to solve many problems) while already having made up their minds about the game and, perhaps unconsciously, overlooked many things that went against this interpretation.<br /> <br /> At least you show a degree of willingness to reapproach the game with an open mind, which is more than many people did and is a commendable effort. But I'm getting tired of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-15-2016, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:46:33-08:00","id":830130,"title":"","content":"I could also tell you that my group of players whose Hunter's PCs are resumable as &quot;assorted jerks who gleefully hunt monsters and sometimes help someone by mistake&quot;, when offered the chance to try Beast, did not create even a single abusive monster. The worst one was &quot;Gordon Gekko meets Smaug&quot; and that's because he was a greedy stockbrocker.<br /> <br /> That should speak volumes. I have the sort of game group that seriously considers the option of using children as a shield when fighting a angry spirit, and yet, their Beasts were all people that tried not to be the monsters they could easily have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:49:34-08:00","id":830133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Feonorx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830098#post830098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thnk you make some very good points, and the feeding examples are quite interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not quite sure I agree, but I can see where you are coming from in regards to the game.<br /> <br /> Speaking of sexual - it is a strange comparison, but I sometimes feel that the gaming community would benefit from the 3 cardinal rules of the BDSM community: Safe, Sane and Consensual. While you can't exactly have a consensual &quot;monster feeding&quot; situation, you can present it in a safe, sane way, if that makes sense...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! I enjoy this kind of conversation, because I always think explaining a topic strengthen one's comprehension of it. As Cinder said, thanks for being open-minded.<br /> <br /> I must say I'm in love with Beast as a game - it's hard to pinpoint a single reason why, but I think its exploration of fear and nightmares is very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:51:46-08:00","id":830134,"title":"","content":"When you're playing a Beast, you are not meant to be an abuser. Feeding your Hunger is more about shock. A sample character is an Anakim Tyrant who works as a health inspector. He gains Satiety by simply being completely irreductible, which shocks restaurant owners that endanger their clients with bad service. The establishment is taken away and people lose jobs, sure, but it prevents people from getting food poisoning.<br /> <br /> You can have a Hunger for Prey while working as a journalist hunting corruption scandals. You can have a straightforward Hunger for Punishment that you can Feed as a police officer or lawyer.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry that you got the impression that this game is just about abusive power fantasies. You're not the first, and you won't be the last.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Listen to Cinder, OP. He has the right idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-15-2016, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T05:33:56-08:00","id":830168,"title":"","content":"Beast deals with some pretty heavy themes, it's true, but while Beasts certainly can be vicious abusers they really aren't forced to.<br /> <br /> Probably the single biggest mechanic that you (and a lot of other people) overlook is Family Dinner. A Beast can tag along with any other supernatural as they replenish their magical fuel and gain Satiety from it. My Anakim character follows his buddies in the Summer Court to political protests and similar events and gets Satiety as they absorb Glamour. It's zero impact feeding, these people were already angry, and arguably doing something productive with that anger. The Changelings get their Glamour, Drake gets his Satiety, and nobody gets hurt because of it. <br /> <br /> Even barring that ability, low Satiety feeding doesn't require you to inflict much if any in the way of lasting mental trauma. The hunger for prey specifically says animals count for low (and only low) Satiety, and the others generally have low impact examples. <br /> <br /> Also, there are a lot of other monsters stalking the night and it's entirely possible to find a role feeding your hunger by protecting people. Drake feeds his hunger for power by fighting the freehold's enemies. Border Reavers, Huntsmen, Charlatans, Loyalists, it doesn't much matter, Drake is prepared to run them off or die trying.<br /> <br /> Another good example from the same setting is Reaper, the city's Apex. She works as an EMT, and she feeds her hunger for prey on the people she saves. Their lives are in her hands, and she uses every bit of her training to save them all, but she gives them just enough of a scare to encourage them to be more careful and appreciate life a little more in the future. Life is precious and fleeting, and second chances are in short supply. When she's not doing that she works with the Autumn Court to patrol the bad parts of town at night, making sure the alleys are safe by scaring away the actual dangers that lurk there. So yeah, she scares a lot of people, which is why she's the Apex, but all of that fear is directed toward raising the average life expectancy of her city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T07:07:51-08:00","id":830212,"title":"","content":"Personally, I appreciate how all of the Chronicles of Darkness games grapple with and engage on topical matters that are horrifying, terrifying, and discomfort causing. That said I'm feeling that there is entirely too much focus on &quot;white hat&quot; vs. &quot;black hat&quot; lately. The whole idea behind these games is that the players are playing monsters. Finding a way to navigate through that is up to the individual troupes. Whatever history you personally have, no game is inherently designed to &quot;do X&quot; in regards to it. It's up to you, your fellow players, and the storyteller to find a good balance.<br /> <br /> From my perspective, I try to never forget that Vampires, Werewolves, and Hunters are murderers, Demons and Changelings trick people out of souls and similar valuables, Mages and Monsters (aka Prometheans) experiment on people for their own ends. All of these are dark misdeeds. All of these splats are horrible, nightmare food. All of these things are damned. Living with damnation is arguably the central theme that all Chronicles of Darkness games have in common. Your hat is black, now what do you do?<br /> <br /> One of the accidental things that the Beast manuscripts have highlighted is just how much <b>trust </b>troupe members need to have with one another to run a game that is going to both engage the game's material and make a fun, enriching experience for everyone involved. Playing these games is not a contest among the players and storyteller, it's a collective exercise in improv group storytelling where everyone has an important, vital part. Beast touches on themes to which we are sensitive to but, if we look, we can see that the other games do too. Mage and Cangeling both deeply engage with madness and mental illness (mostly because we still perceive that there's something wrong with folks who don't perceive the world the way we do). Vampire and Werewolf also have linkages to the theme of abuse (consider the enslaving effects of vitae addiction and the life of a blood doll or consider how werewolves determine and maintain the pecking order in a pack).<br /> <br /> As has been pointed out by many of the posters in this thread there are several mechanics which equip storytellers and players to tell multiple kinds of stories using the game's systems (even if they're not perfect systems). While abuse and the effects of it are major themes in the game, the game is also (roughly) equipped replace its own themes with those from any of the other gamelines (using effects like Kinship and Family Dinner, even where they're not perfect).<br /> <br /> As always though, the developers have delivered a sandbox toolkit and it's up to individual troupes to fashion from it the kind of story they want to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 02-15-2016, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T08:34:48-08:00","id":830251,"title":"","content":"I appreciate that you all are taking this in the tone I intended and not that tone that may have come across. Yes, this is an emotional topic for me, and I appreciate the understanding that that has been shown. <br /> <br /> I'm glad that the latest (final?) version is much revised. That is very reassuring to me. I also appreciate where people pointed out where and how the rules allow the worst aspects can be worked around, such as the Family Dinner, which I freely admit I missed on previous readings. The ways to make a heroic character are very interesting and eye-opening. I look forward to seeing the final product, and seeing how much it has changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T09:02:44-08:00","id":830262,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, Fearnox, the opening post really struck me the wrong way. It was not pleasant and I've been thinking about it since this morning. I get that the topic hits you close to home but it sure was not the best way to express your doubts and made some accusations about Beast fans that I did not liked in the slightest. That's why I adopted an aggressive tone that's very far from the way I usually try to answer people.<br /> <br /> Still, as I said, I appreciate that under it there is a genuine desire to learn more and see how much Beast can work around your issues with some of its aspects. That is a willingness to give a second chance (a deserved one, I'd say) to this game that I can only wish more people had. For that, kudos.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that the discussion proved useful and helped you see things under a different light.<br /> <br /> Let me close with a Skyrim quote that I feel it's relevant:<br /> <br /> &quot;What is better - to be born good, or to overcome your evil nature through great effort?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not perfect for Beast, but it fits a facet of the core moral drama reasonably well, at least the one we're discussing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T09:55:04-08:00","id":830282,"title":"","content":"Well, Cinder, I can see how it could come across that way. I read the Preview edition, stewed for a while, and then posted. That post was re-written probably a dozen times, toning it down with each iteration. Maybe I should have re-written a few dozen more, but I very much appreciate that people took the intent behind it and overlooked/forgave my venting that bled through. That in and of itself went a long ways toward my decision to give the final product another look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T10:52:14-08:00","id":830322,"title":"","content":"Yeah, well, from my part I'm sorry. I'm not sure how much my post proved useful to you specifically and, while I tried to address your concerns, I realize that the tone could have been better.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T11:21:42-08:00","id":830353,"title":"","content":"Bah, both of us had questionable tone covering good intentions. No blood, no foul and a good discussion was generated that I (at least) learned from. I don't necessarily agree with all that was said (Jacob, I'm looking at you here) but I appreciate the alternate viewpoints and good information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T11:34:57-08:00","id":830363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Feonorx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830084#post830084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for your example, I not sure that what you describe would work per the rules, as he is not Satiating on people. Further, if that counts as heroism, I'm not sure we are working off the same definitions. Perhaps if he used his instinctive urge to hunt and chase on Vampires, evil cultists, or what-have-you then maybe... but would he be generating sufficient terror to fill the Hunger? Not sure it would work...</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the actual rules printed, a Predator can feed on animals just fine so long as her Satiety is low. And feeding on vampires, evil cultists and what have you actually gets you WAY more Satiety than feeding on regular humans on account of being much more difficult and requiring a lot more involvement and planning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T14:07:09-08:00","id":830501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830262#post830262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me close with a Skyrim quote that I feel it's relevant:<br /> <br /> &quot;What is better - to be born good, or to overcome your evil nature through great effort?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not perfect for Beast, but it fits a facet of the core moral drama reasonably well, at least the one we're discussing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Piggybacking on this to more fully quote a bit that I've <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811820#post811820\">previously mentioned</a> thinking fits the general conceit reasonably well:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jules Winnfield, Pulp Fiction</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ezekiel 25:17. &quot;The path of the righteous man is beset on all sides by the iniquities of the selfish and the tyranny of evil men. Blessed is he who, in the name of charity and good will, shepherds the weak through the valley of darkness, for he is truly his brother's keeper and the finder of lost children. And I will strike down upon thee with great vengeance and furious anger those who attempt to poison and destroy my brothers. And you will know my name is the Lord when I lay my vengeance upon thee.&quot;<br /> <br /> I been saying that shit for years. And if you heard it, that meant your ass. I never gave much thought to what it meant. I just thought it was some cold-blooded shit to say to a motherfucker before I popped a cap in his ass.<br /> <br /> But I saw some shit this morning made me think twice. See, now I'm thinking, maybe it means you're the evil man, and I'm the righteous man, and Mr. 9 Millimeter here? He's the shepherd protecting my righteous ass in the valley of darkness. Or it could mean you're the righteous man and I'm the shepherd and it's the world that's evil and selfish. Now I'd like that. But that shit ain't the truth.<br /> <br /> <b>The truth is\u2026you're the weak, and I am the tyranny of evil men. But I'm trying, Ringo. I'm trying <u>real hard</u> to be the shepherd.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T14:15:31-08:00","id":830506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830501#post830501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Piggybacking on this to more fully quote a bit that I've <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811820#post811820\">previously mentioned</a> thinking fits the general conceit reasonably well:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciated that reference the first time you made it and it still has all my support. It encapsulates the struggle of Beasts that attempt to do good perfectly.<br /> <br /> It also refers to a sort of character arc that I personally love (there's a sample Efreet in my Djinn thread which was written after a viewing of Pulp Fiction and is blatantly based on Jules), but that belongs more to the realm of personal preferences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:10:18-08:00","id":830619,"title":"","content":"Oh yay, another thing I need to respond to.<br /> <br /> My plate's getting a little full here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:27:27-08:00","id":830630,"title":"","content":"I would respond but I think any point I would make and every proposition I would question have been brought up already in a more than satisfactory manner, and I'm a little weary of the topic from the discussions during the course of the kickstarter and immediately after. (&lt;,&lt;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:34:59-08:00","id":830636,"title":"","content":"I feel older just thinking about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:51:18-08:00","id":830644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830619#post830619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yay, another thing I need to respond to.<br /> <br /> My plate's getting a little full here.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the OP, no need to on my part. While I would love to hear your opinion, I think the others have convinced me that my reaction to the Preview was<br /> <br /> A) probably a bit of over-reaction in hindsight<br /> and<br /> B) not necessarily reflective of the changes in further versions<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely curious to see how the final version comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":11143,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","user":"Feonorx","date":". 02-15-2016, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:52:44-08:00","id":830645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830134#post830134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have a straightforward Hunger for Punishment that you can Feed as a police officer or lawyer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, that's somehow the least reassuring sentiment offered in this entire thread, and I agree that Beast is wildly misconstrued by people on the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T18:46:39-08:00","id":830671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830636#post830636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel older just thinking about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Want to feel even older?<br /> Wait. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T18:52:42-08:00","id":830678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830645#post830645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, that's somehow the least reassuring sentiment offered in this entire thread, and I agree that Beast is wildly misconstrued by people on the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div> I apologize if it didn't help as much as I expected. Other users have made very good points on their defense of the game, so I'm not worried.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T18:58:49-08:00","id":830682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830678#post830678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I apologize if it didn't help as much as I expected. Other users have made very good points on their defense of the game, so I'm not worried.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was slightly kidding. It was really just the idea of the sort of institutional, systematic power wielded and misused by perfectly mundane humans in those professions is already terrifying, nevermind someone who would feel supernaturally compelled to push at the boundaries of what is acceptable in those professions anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T20:53:06-08:00","id":830772,"title":"","content":"Well for examples of other ways to feed that don't cause direct trauma.<br /> Nick Knight Ugallu Collector<br /> Nick Collects victims, his day job is a psychologist on call with Chicago SVU.<br /> <br /> <br /> the simple fact is In Nick's case he doesn't have to raise a hand to anyone and doesn't inflict a serious trauma on anyone what he does is he takes away someone's victim, and with it their power of that person. Nick is the example of a benevolent beast, who helps others. He teaches those who would harm others that eventually you will lose this power over your wife/lover/child/who ever it is and you will lose them too. Someone will come along and take away your toy, and you will have a face a world without them a world that will hate you (i.e. Prison).<br /> <br /> Another example collector I experienced was a Gencon. This collector was also a psychologist. He collected people's stories. Had them talk about their problems and collected the stories, the things that were hurting them, as they let go of these things it helped them.<br /> <br /> Also at Gencon we had a actress Anakim who was a total diva and had to have her way. By throwing around her stardom and clout with her directors and co-workers she was able to feed. Just remember the &quot;Shock&quot; doesn't have to be traumatic it can be therapeutic as well. Sometimes it can be as simple as &quot;No brown M&amp;M's in the dressing room.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T01:29:02-08:00","id":830898,"title":"","content":"I for one really enjoyed the conversation which came out of this - perhaps because I missed some of the debates when the game first came out - and I'm glad the OP posted his doubts, and was honest in confronting them. Maybe it's because I come from the L5R fandom (where EVERYONE is RIGHT ALL THE TIME) but I appreciate the level of maturity shown in this thread.<br /> <br /> Another good point which has been raised above is the ability to feed from supernatural beings, or even animals. There are plenty of baddies in the Chronicles of Darkness settings which could use a good fright. Even if you leave out the morally gray ones (such as a vampire who doesn't kill while feeding, or a werewolf who doesn't cause unnecessary harm) you still have draugrs, centimani, spirits, the Pure, True Faes, Tremeres, stryx (stirxes? Strygoi? Strox?)... not easy prey, but as said above, even more rewarding because of it.<br /> <br /> Extra thought: does anything stop a beast from preying on other beasts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:46:45-08:00","id":831023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div 