he's driven mad with regret, feeling she cannot hope to live her life until she slays him, her friends, family, all of them suffer until she follows through with this cruel Geas thrust upon her. Such is the lamentation of the Tragic Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T13:24:57-08:00","id":833992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=833856#post833856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think that Heroes as just as much capable of Good as well as Evil. In one case, maybe it's not that the Hero WANTS to kill the Beast, it's just she has no choice. Perhaps like in the Movie Unbreakable, Fate continues to force the Hero into scenarios where she cannot hope to do anything but combat the Beast, even if she sees him as her friend or loved one. Perhaps she's driven mad with regret, feeling she cannot hope to live her life until she slays him, her friends, family, all of them suffer until she follows through with this cruel Geas thrust upon her. Such is the lamentation of the Tragic Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>PG 202 of the update. Essentially Heroes are drawn to disruptions in the Primordial Dream with a desire to fix the disruption. If a Beast is the cause of said disruption then the Hero is probably going to try and kill the Beast, however Beasts aren't always the problem and many a hero will still be trying to fix those problems regardless. Hell the book even points out that you'll get Heroes who don't even know Beasts exist and just go around trying to help with the problems because they're drawn to fix things when they feel something is wrong. <br /> <br /> It's just that the Hero who shows up to a city ravaged by a natural disaster, because they felt the problems caused needed to be addressed and has decided to help with in whatever way they can, is less of an antagonist to a Beast than the one who's convinced the Beast is an unholy abomination against all that is and the best option is to dismember the carcass, burn it to ash, and scatter the ashes to the cardinal directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T13:38:58-08:00","id":834009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=833992#post833992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PG 202 of the update. Essentially Heroes are drawn to disruptions in the Primordial Dream with a desire to fix the disruption. If a Beast is the cause of said disruption then the Hero is probably going to try and kill the Beast, however Beasts aren't always the problem and many a hero will still be trying to fix those problems regardless. Hell the book even points out that you'll get Heroes who don't even know Beasts exist and just go around trying to help with the problems because they're drawn to fix things when they feel something is wrong. <br /> <br /> It's just that the Hero who shows up to a city ravaged by a natural disaster, because they felt the problems caused needed to be addressed and has decided to help with in whatever way they can, is less of an antagonist to a Beast than the one who's convinced the Beast is an unholy abomination against all that is and the best option is to dismember the carcass, burn it to ash, and scatter the ashes to the cardinal directions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's entirely possible that there are dozens of Heroes in the Doctors Without Borders, drawn to the fear of disease and war in developing countries and who feel the need to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:01:56-08:00","id":835005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Feonorx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil#post830051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, at the behest of some people's comments in another thread I tracked down the Preview PDF that is available to the public to read the Heroes information. I figured I would read the whole thing just to get a feel for how it works an- HOLY CRAP WHAT THE F*CK IS WRONG WITH YOU PEOPLE?!?!<br /> <br /> As a survivor of mental and emotional abuse from a predator pretending to be a loving family member, what I read horrified me to my core. It seems that, if I was reading it right, Beasts *must* inflict some kind of pain on their neighbors to feed their &quot;special souls&quot;. In essence Beasts are abusers but they seem to justify it by targeting people who 'deserve' it. Oh, god, that is not going to sound familiar to abuse survivors AT ALL.<br /> <br /> Now, I have been playing RPG's since the early-80's. Odds are if a game has come out in the last 30-years or so I've played it. I've played lot of Horror RPG's of various types, I've even played some of the oWoD Black Dog label games and worse. But this game practically requires the players to learn how to and play out doing deep psychological damage and long term mental scarring as part of the basic game mechanic.<br /> <br /> I understand that the authors/moderators (at least the two I have interacted with so far) have a rather non &quot;black and white&quot; sense of morality, but a game where you are tormenting people with your fantastical dragon soul and if people object to it then they are evil bigots who don't understand you seems to be beyond &quot;playing a monster&quot; and possibly reaching &quot;Inherently Evil&quot;. This certainly seems to be beyond where the other &quot;monster&quot; game lines go to. When vampires skew evil, for example, they typically see themselves as apex predators; <i>detached</i> predators. If you look at the Invictus or the Sanctum they have opinions about human masses and not individual people. We still can acknowledge that as an evil perspective but it's sensible. I think it's the fact that Beasts tend to judge their prey on a very personal, often petty scale that would make even a vampire raise an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> As TVTropes puts it, &quot;Beasts <i>cannot</i> avoid their need to feed. Even the weakest of Beasts, those who cling most strongly to their human origins, have a choice: either deliberately find someone and scare them, as appropriate for their Hunger, once per week, or else cause nightmares in random people, which will potentially create some loony who will happily maim, kill and burn innocent bystanders to find and kill them. The &quot;best&quot; Beasts are those who accept their Hunger and find a way to sate it that minimizes the harm they cause, as several sample characters mentioned in the corebook show.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now you can try to justify the seeding of fear and apprehension as a good thing - giving people something to overcome and better themselves, etc - but THAT IS LITERALLY THEY TYPE OF THING THAT REAL-LIFE ABUSERS SAY TO JUSTIFY THEIR ATROCITIES. Even the powers, with names like &quot;Everyone Hates You,&quot; &quot;You Deserve This,&quot; and &quot;Everything You Do is Worthless&quot; read like the a laundry-list of psychosis-causing phraseology. The players know from the very beginning that they are truly evil creatures intended to cause horror, regardless of how they try to justify it or minimize their harm. Heroes, for all their fanaticism and flaws, are trying to stop a self-admitted monster from spreading nightmares across... well.. everywhere but somehow Beasts have the moral high ground?<br /> <br /> At least one poster in the other threat suggested that Beasts, while monsters, could be heroes. Having now read the book I literally do not see how that is possible. I may be missing something but this might as well have been called Sadist: the Abuser instead. Now, I will admit that, given my background, I am not exactly coming to this game with no baggage. SO...<br /> <br /> Explain to me how sounds like a fun experience which will totally not bring the wrong kind of attention.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Well actually, Beasts torment people because they feed on fear. And they don't have to inflict bodily harm on the subject to get it. Only Predators (hunger for blood) need to do so, and even then they don't actually have to kill. Just wound them a bit.<br /> <br /> Beasts also don't have much choice in the matter. If they try to starve their soul, it goes on a rampage whether they like it or not. At least by feeding it, they can control its impulses instead of letting it attack everything in sight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The reason why Heroes are &quot;evil&quot; is not because they want to kill Beasts, it's because they are <b>obsessed with killing Beasts</b> and they want to take all the glory for it. Heroes are the things Hunters are afraid of becoming, somebody who hunts monsters because they want admiration, not because they care about humanity. A Hero will justify any excuse as long as it results in killing the monster... even sacrificing human lives!<br /> <br /> <br /> The concept of good and evil is not as clear cut as &quot;I hurt people, I'm evil&quot; or &quot;I help people, I'm good.&quot; A person who is evil hurts people because <i>they want </i>to hurt people. A person who is good helps people because <i>they want</i> to help people. Beasts don't have a choice in the matter, <i>they need</i> to hurt people, and bad things happen to them if they do not. I don't know if you've ever read Johnny the Homicidal Maniac, but his story is very similar to that of a Beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the story, Johnny is forced to paint a wall of his house with fresh human blood on a regular basis. If he stops doing so, the collective madness of mankind will burst forth from it and begin attacking everything in sight. We later find out he's something called a &quot;waste lock&quot; who's duty is to keep the madness locked away.<br /> <br /> <br /> Classic World of Darkness focused on a meta plot between the stories, but New World of Darkness is more focused on your character having become a monster and is now learning how to cope with that situation. nWoD is a game about personal horror and moral choices, not epic showdowns on top skyscrapers or battling ancient deities rising from their tombs. Your character is cursed, but whether you fight against the curse, or let it consume you depends on how you handle the situation.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-22-2016, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:18:03-08:00","id":835022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=835005#post835005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Well actually, Beasts torment people because they feed on fear. And they don't have to inflict bodily harm on the subject to get it. Only Predators (hunger for blood) need to do so, and even then they don't actually have to kill. Just wound them a bit.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Even Predators don't actually need to hurt people. Social Predators are fairly common. Hell, a Predator could feed at low Satiety by dumping successive girlfriends after saying that they were the only one for them. That's hardly extreme harm or abuse. it's not <i>good</i>, but it's not inhumanly cruel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:24:14-08:00","id":835031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=835022#post835022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even Predators don't actually need to hurt people. Social Predators are fairly common. Hell, a Predator could feed at low Satiety by dumping successive girlfriends after saying that they were the only one for them. That's hardly extreme harm or abuse. it's not <i>good</i>, but it's not inhumanly cruel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, didn't remember until after I wrote it that Predators just need their victims to feel like prey in order to satiate themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> But on the subject of a hero Beast, there's the Nemeses who hunger for punishment. Which could very easily be turned into a street side vigilante who scares the hell out of criminals in his city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:43:44-08:00","id":835042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830092#post830092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> : funny, the waitress thing happened in the very first scene of my campaign.<br /> <br /> Also, if you want a popular example of a heroic beast... there's Batman. The man uses fear as his weapon, to discourage crime. It's his tool, and he probably gets off on it way more than he should - but at the end of the day, if it keeps criminals from doing worse things, it can be counted as a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Does it... does it really? Batman stops a bunch of street level thugs who are just trying to make some quick cash. Meanwhile, the psychopaths who commit mass murder are taken off to Gotham's revolving door prison system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:49:55-08:00","id":835048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=835042#post835042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it... does it really? Batman stops a bunch of street level thugs who are just trying to make some quick cash. Meanwhile, the psychopaths who commit mass murder are taken off to Gotham's revolving door prison system.</div> </div> </div> </div>He stops the psychopaths from committing mass murder, too, is the thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:59:38-08:00","id":835053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=835048#post835048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He stops the psychopaths from committing mass murder, too, is the thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And they're certainly scared of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T08:01:57-08:00","id":835054,"title":"","content":"Even an Incarnate's Myth could be a kind of urban myth or the sort of story that parents tell their children to keep them in the house at night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T08:15:56-08:00","id":835065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=835053#post835053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And they're certainly scared of him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not scared enough to stop and learn their lesson, though. Even the weaker villains keep picking fights with him, hoping they'll get lucky the next time around. If anything, it seems Batman is going easy on them so he has a constant food supply.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T08:18:03-08:00","id":835067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=835065#post835065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not scared enough to stop and learn their lesson, though. Even the weaker villains keep picking fights with him, hoping they'll get lucky the next time around. If anything, it seems Batman is going easy on them so he has a constant food supply.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems sensible to me. No sense in making it so you can only feed from a given person once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T09:38:49-08:00","id":835111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=835067#post835067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Seems sensible to me. No sense in making it so you can only feed from a given person once.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So he's a Beast on a diet. plenty of left overs in the fridge! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"",